# ⛔⛔ WITHOUT THIS FILE THE BUILD CONTEXT IS 26 GB.
#
# `puzzle/Dockerfile` COPIES repo-root-relative paths (`tlon/`, `tools/`,
# `puzzle/`, `runs/puzzle_speaker/dosed-s20624/`), so the build context has to
# be the repository root. The root holds `runs/` — every adapter, corpus, probe
# ledger and log this project has ever produced — and Docker uploads the whole
# context before it reads the first COPY. The image needs 309 MB of that.
#
# ⛔ THE FAILURE IS SLOW AND EXPENSIVE, WHICH IS WHY IT IS WORTH A FILE. A 26 GB
# upload does not fail fast; it crawls, and then times out after a long time
# spent looking like progress. Nothing about the Dockerfile would look wrong.

# ── everything under runs/, then the one cell the image serves back ─────────
# ⛔ ORDER AND GRANULARITY BOTH MATTER. Docker cannot re-include a path whose
# PARENT is excluded, so the directories are opened one level at a time rather
# than with a single `!runs/puzzle_speaker/dosed-s20624/` after `runs/`.
# ⛔ The cell name is spelt here as well as in the Dockerfile and
# `tests/test_puzzle_serves_v1.py`. `tests/test_puzzle_build_context.py` pins
# them together, because an adapter swap that missed this file would exclude
# the weights and the image would silently ship without them — and
# `Speaker.load()` refuses on a missing adapter, so it would fail at boot on a
# machine that had already been paid for and deployed.
runs/*
!runs/puzzle_speaker/
runs/puzzle_speaker/*
!runs/puzzle_speaker/dosed-s20624/

# ── the rest of the repository the image does not serve ────────────────────
.git/
.github/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
tests/
spec/
docs/
scratchpad/
*.md
!puzzle/README.md

# ⛔ Never. These are credentials and local machine state, and a build context
# is not a private channel — every layer is readable by anyone who can pull the
# image.
.env
.env.*
**/INSTANCE.json
**/IP.txt
*.sqlite3
